    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ubvbc9l",
      "content": "Latitudes and longitudes form the geographical coordinate system used to locate places on the Earth's surface. Latitudes run east–west and measure distance north or south of the Equator, while longitudes run north–south and measure distance east or west of the Prime Meridian.<img></img>"
    },
