    {
      "id": "7lsz0rq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Latitudes"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Latitudes are parallel circles running horizontally East to West, measuring distance North or South of the Equator (0°).",
        "Longitudes are vertical meridians running North to South from pole to pole, measuring distance East or West of the Prime Meridian (0°).",
        "Indian Standard Time (IST) is calculated along the 82.5° E longitude passing through Mirzapur, Uttar Pradesh.",
        "The Tropic of Cancer (23.5° N) passes through 8 Indian states: Gujarat, Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh, Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, West Bengal, Tripura, and Mizoram.",
        "The Equator (0° latitude) passes through three major continents: South America, Africa, and Asia."
      ],
      "id": "aalke5b"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pytjiuf",
      "content": "• Latitudes are imaginary lines drawn parallel to the Equator. "
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o3dwwvd",
      "content": "• They measure distance north or south of the Equator."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "23rhd96",
      "content": "• The Equator is 0° latitude."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "16zpktl",
      "content": "• Latitudes extend from 0° to 90° North and 0° to 90° South."
    },
    {
      "id": "p2estka",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Important Latitudes"
